Decide whether the proposed member claims can be represented by one display fact.

A display fact is one concise sentence shown on the supplied subject's wiki page. Mark the group `equivalent` when all
member claims assert the same subject, event or state, time, and material details in alternative wording, so any one
member claim can represent the group without losing information. Mark it `composable` when the claims add distinct,
compatible details that can faithfully coexist in one sentence. Mark it `split_required` when the claims record
distinct memories or could describe separate occurrences and should become separate display facts.

Do not write the display sentence or change claim content. Return one schema-valid verdict for the supplied fact key.
